WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:57.470
<b>Adventure on Little Garden</b>

3
00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:14.680
Aw, no snow. Too bad.

4
00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.110
Snow, in this climate?

5
00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.450
Sure, why not?
Already happened once.

6
00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.990
You just missed it
cause you were asleep.

7
00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:23.760
Hey! What about you?
Do you think it's gonna snow?

8
00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:24.960
I wouldn't rule anything out.

9
00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.670
But the sea you were
in the first time

10
00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:28.520
it snowed was special.

11
00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.100
The seven magnetic fields that
emit from Reverse Mountain

12
00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:33.940
tend to make things
particularly chaotic.

13
00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.910
But that doesn't mean
you should relax your guard

14
00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:40.710
while sailing these waters.

15
00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:44.810
The odds of it being as wild as
your first journey may be small.

16
00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.630
Still, these waters
aren't normal

17
00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:49.320
and are certain to hold
surprises of their own.

18
00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.720
Remember: Never
underestimate this sea.

19
00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.560
Hey, guys!

20
00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:57.790
Anyone care to sample
my special drink?

21
00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:01.900
Woo-hoo!

22
00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:11.770
Hey, you guys want to
get out the fishing gear?

23
00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:13.800
Fishing! Hell yeah. I'm in!

24
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:14.900
Sounds good to me!

25
00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.070
I'll even make you one of
my custom fishing rods!

26
00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.610
You'll love it!

27
00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:22.900
Wow, somebody's
sure thirsty. Have another.

28
00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.010
The sounds he makes
when he slurps are hilarious!

29
00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:29.180
Yeah, give him another one.

30
00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:32.110
They're acting like idiots!

31
00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:33.540
Maybe this will help.

32
00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.010
Uh?

33
00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:36.040
Just relax.

34
00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.210
These boys may go through
their goofy phases,

35
00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.680
but when things get rough,
they get to work.

36
00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.720
Trust me. I should know.

37
00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.720
Sorry. I don't know
what's wrong with me.

38
00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.220
I'm getting worked
up over nothing.

39
00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:52.190
This ship will put you at ease.
You'll cheer up in no time!

40
00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.420
Attaboy!

41
00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.090
Go, go, go, go, go, go, go!

42
00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.200
Yeah. They're... funny.

43
00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.050
Hey look, it's a dolphin!
Pirate's best friend!

44
00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.830
Whoa! Beautiful!

45
00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:36.050
– It's huge!
– It's huge!

46
00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.000
Let's go!

47
00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:52.640
Move it!

48
00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:53.340
Okay!

49
00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.910
Going!

50
00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:01.530
Got it!

51
00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:02.400
Take that side!

52
00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.730
Gotcha!

53
00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:05.100
She was right!

54
00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.570
Okay, hurry! Let's move!

55
00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:22.340
Get ready.
It's gonna be a big one!

56
00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.150
Nami! Which direction now?

57
00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.620
Gimme a second. I'll check.

58
00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:48.200
Port side... full!

59
00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:52.270
– Turning full!
– Turning full!

60
00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:13.190
There's no mistake.

61
00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:15.550
Cactus Island and this one here

62
00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:19.410
are definitely pulling
against each other.

63
00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.040
Our next stop!

64
00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:36.760
This is it! Our second
island in the Grand Line!

65
00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:50.600
<b>Vacation Island
The Grand Line</b>

66
00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:57.100
Mr. 3.

67
00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.850
Yes, my dear. Hold on.

68
00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:01.020
Ahh.

69
00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:04.790
There's nothing quite like
the rich aroma of Earl Grey.

70
00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:06.610
I'm bored.

71
00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:08.760
On the one hand,
you say you're bored.

72
00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:11.500
On the other, you don't
like working. Correct?

73
00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.600
Mm-hmm.

74
00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:13.600
Then why don't you
cease your complaining

75
00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.770
and revel in the enjoyment
of this rare slice

76
00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:18.800
of freedom circumstances have
generously afforded you?

77
00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.930
How grand to be able
to take a long vacation.

78
00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:24.970
A privilege few officers
ever get to indulge.

79
00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:26.670
One more thing...

80
00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:31.850
<b>Mr. 3
Officer Agent, Baroque Works</b>

81
00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.340
I would appreciate your mindful
and immediate discretion

82
00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:32.280
in not calling me by
my code name in public.

83
00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:36.060
Otherwise, people will discover
that I am indeed Mr. 3.

84
00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:41.480
<b>Miss Golden Week
Officer Agent, Baroque Works</b>

85
00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:39.780
Sure.

86
00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.910
Mm...

87
00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:43.750
Incidentally, I couldn't
help noticing

88
00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:45.320
you've been perusing
that piece of paper

89
00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:48.390
over the last several days.
Why does it grab you so?

90
00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:49.820
It's an order from Boss.

91
00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:52.410
Why didn't you
tell me sooner?!

92
00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:59.470
It says Mr. 5 has
been taken down.

93
00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.040
If someone had to
be terminated,

94
00:08:01.110 --> 00:08:03.950
I wish it would've been
someone useless like Mr. 2.

95
00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.440
So it would benefit you.

96
00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:07.140
With a fat promotion.

97
00:08:07.140 --> 00:08:08.450
It's not that, necessarily.

98
00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:12.180
Rather, the downfall of Mr. 5
is hardly exciting news at all.

99
00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:14.480
The man excelled at nothing
but his own idiocy,

100
00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:18.660
clinging to his devil fruit
Power like a drowning rat.

101
00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:21.460
You are correct that a modicum
of my indifference stems from

102
00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:23.990
the fact that 5's misfortune
brings me no gain.

103
00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:24.960
All we may learn is

104
00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:28.570
power means nothing if
not properly harnessed.

105
00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.520
Superior
criminals are those

106
00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:37.390
who execute their crimes
using superior intellect.

107
00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:41.060
Nevertheless, whoever beat Mr.
5 should be made an example of,

108
00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.190
if for no other reason than
to preserve the reputation

109
00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:46.290
of terror our organization has
painstakingly cultivated,

110
00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:49.130
and indeed for criminality
as a whole.

111
00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:02.430
I can see why they call
this place Little Garden!

112
00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.270
I can't.
What's "little" about it?!

113
00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:07.440
Yeah, this island looks
pretty harsh if you ask me.

114
00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.470
Why the cute name?

115
00:09:08.470 --> 00:09:11.840
Y-Y-Yeah, it looks
like a jungle out there!

116
00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:13.580
Maybe we'd be better
off skipping this one.

117
00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:14.810
We have to be careful.

118
00:09:14.810 --> 00:09:19.070
I can't help but remember the
warning Miss All Sunday gave us.

119
00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:22.740
So what, we might be attacked
by giant monsters?!

120
00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:23.940
Heh! Who knows?

121
00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:25.770
Listen, I'm sure we can
make it to the next island

122
00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:27.610
without going ashore
on this one!

123
00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:30.180
The only way to reset
the log is to go ashore.

124
00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:31.750
Not to mention we're
in dire need

125
00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:33.620
of re-stocking our food supply.

126
00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:36.620
We didn't get so much as a sack
of flour in the last town.

127
00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:39.790
Guys! There's our ticket in.

128
00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:40.790
Huh?

129
00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:47.440
Think they'll have a
barbecue restaurant here?

130
00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.570
We didn't travel
all this way for barbecue!

131
00:09:49.570 --> 00:09:51.600
I thought the point
of this visit was to get food?

132
00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.070
Food as in supplies
we're going to cook later!

133
00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:55.780
Jeez, what're you thinking?

134
00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:56.620
I don't know.

135
00:09:56.620 --> 00:10:00.490
Usopp might be right
about this one.

136
00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.220
Just take a look at the
gargantuan plant life here.

137
00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.850
I've never seen anything
like it, not even in books.

138
00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:13.880
You're so adorable!

139
00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:15.850
Thank you!

140
00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:18.390
That's not funny!
I was talking to Nami!

141
00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.250
What was that screeching?!

142
00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:24.260
It's all right, love.
It's only a bird.

143
00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.280
Perfectly harmless.
Just like this jungle.

144
00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:27.310
Nothin' to worry about.

145
00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:31.980
Uh... What's wrong?

146
00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:40.240
What the hell's the
matter with you, ya damn bird?!

147
00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.810
Ooh. It's big. Could be tasty.

148
00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.060
Hear that?! Is that
the kinda noise

149
00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:52.120
you expect to hear
in a normal jungle?!

150
00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:54.320
That sounded like
a volcano erupting!

151
00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.010
We're all going to die!

152
00:11:07.900 --> 00:11:08.900
A tiger?!

153
00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:11.440
It's gigantic!

154
00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:15.150
Uh!

155
00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:22.710
What?! Luffy, what
just happened?!

156
00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:26.040
I know normal!
This is definitely not it!

157
00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.770
Someone explain to me
how a mammoth tiger

158
00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.430
can just keel over
covered in blood!

159
00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:34.570
Log-Pose and food be damned!

160
00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:37.430
We're not stepping foot on
that island and that's final!

161
00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:39.570
We can still reset the
readings on the ship.

162
00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:41.270
We'll just sit tight until then.

163
00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:43.740
When that's done, we'll
leave and never look back!

164
00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:44.610
Great!

165
00:11:44.610 --> 00:11:48.290
Yeah. Great. We'll
all just stay here!

166
00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.240
Sanji, go make lunch!

167
00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:00.740
You want lunch?

168
00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:02.640
Yep, and one more thing!

169
00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:04.090
Make it a great big
"pirate lunch"...

170
00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:06.580
with lots of meat
and no veggies!

171
00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.810
I'm going to need
some more energy!

172
00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:10.310
Uh! Energy for what?!

173
00:12:10.310 --> 00:12:12.650
What are you doing?!
You're not leaving here!

174
00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:14.150
You know! Heh, heh!

175
00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:16.320
Fun stuff! Do ya
wanna come along?

176
00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:19.530
It's useless. I can't stop him.

177
00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:20.930
He's too enthusiastic.

178
00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:22.120
Is he crazy?!

179
00:12:22.120 --> 00:12:24.050
Somewhere out there is
a monster big enough

180
00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:26.600
to grind a tiger into paste!

181
00:12:26.600 --> 00:12:28.310
Sanji! I'm starving!

182
00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.760
Right. Be patient.

183
00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:31.590
I'll have it to you
as soon as I can.

184
00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:35.610
Say, Luffy!

185
00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:37.270
Would it be all right if
I come along with you?

186
00:12:38.100 --> 00:12:39.270
Sure! Sounds great!

187
00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:41.870
No! Vivi, you can't be serious!

188
00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:43.690
Yeah. I'd rather not sit here

189
00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:46.110
with nothing to do but
worry about my troubles.

190
00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.380
This will keep me busy
until the log's reset.

191
00:12:48.380 --> 00:12:50.150
Out of the question! Seriously!

192
00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:52.280
It's way too dangerous
for you out there!

193
00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:55.890
I'll be fine. Besides,
I'll have Karoo with me.

194
00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:00.660
Hey something's wrong.
Karoo doesn't look too good.

195
00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:01.660
He might be in shock.

196
00:13:01.660 --> 00:13:03.830
Vivi, if you go exploring,
you'll need to eat.

197
00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:04.900
I'll pack you a lunch.

198
00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:06.000
Thanks.

199
00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.100
While you're at it, could you
fix something for Karoo?

200
00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:11.570
Of course! You just
leave it to me!

201
00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:17.650
Okay.

202
00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:25.710
Now you're all set
and ready to go!

203
00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:27.770
Two pirate lunches
for Luffy and Vivi,

204
00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:29.430
and a special drink for Karoo!

205
00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.200
Heh! Thanks.

206
00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:38.810
Well. See you guys later!

207
00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:42.040
Don't worry!
Everything will be fine!

208
00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:46.080
Vivi. What a girl.
She's so brave.

209
00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:47.880
And just what would
you expect from someone

210
00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.250
who could infiltrate
the enemy's ranks.

211
00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:55.110
I'm bored.
I'm gonna take a walk.

212
00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:56.070
Take a walk?!

213
00:13:59.220 --> 00:14:02.660
Uh! Hey! Zoro! Wait up!

214
00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:03.630
Hm?

215
00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:05.600
You know we're kinda
short on food, right?

216
00:14:05.600 --> 00:14:08.500
If you find any animals that
appear edible, bring'em back.

217
00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:10.240
Okay, that's easy.

218
00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.300
I could see why you'd want
to send me, cause I can

219
00:14:12.300 --> 00:14:14.510
bring back somethin' you
couldn't catch yourself.

220
00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:16.480
What the hell
does that mean?!

221
00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:20.450
I won't let that
remark go unchallenged!

222
00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:22.980
You're saying you can capture
bigger game than I can?

223
00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:26.180
Like my hunting skills
are inferior?!

224
00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:28.020
Yeah, that's right.

225
00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:35.160
Challenge accepted.

226
00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:41.630
Okay! Winner brings back
the most pounds of meat.

227
00:14:41.630 --> 00:14:44.070
Whaddaya mean pounds,
'cause I'll bring back tons?!

228
00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:46.320
Why don't you let your
hunting do your talking for you.

229
00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:48.240
Heh. Good luck, cook!

230
00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:51.560
I will never understand it.

231
00:14:51.560 --> 00:14:54.200
Why do those two jerks have
to be so competitive?

232
00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.130
Don't cry. If it makes
you feel better,

233
00:14:56.130 --> 00:14:58.970
I'm just as stumped by
their behavior as you.

234
00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:05.470
We're sitting ducks.

235
00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:08.380
Don't you think I
already know that?!

236
00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:14.900
Why didn't I think
of that before?!

237
00:15:14.900 --> 00:15:17.070
Uh?! Where are you going?!

238
00:15:18.300 --> 00:15:20.340
Nami, what's wrong?!

239
00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:23.060
Mm. That's not it...
Mm... Not this one either.

240
00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:24.290
– Nope.

241
00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:25.090
Nami! Whoa! Hey!

242
00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:28.280
What the heck are you
looking for anyway?! Huh?!

243
00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.180
Quiet!

244
00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:31.410
I remember reading
about it in a book.

245
00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:33.540
Uh. Reading about what?

246
00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:34.870
Little Garden.

247
00:15:38.680 --> 00:15:39.780
Hey, what's the matter?

248
00:15:39.780 --> 00:15:41.450
Over here! Check it out!

249
00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:44.550
It's a shellfish that
looks like a squid.

250
00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:49.090
Shell squidfish! Heh, heh!

251
00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:49.890
How strange.

252
00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:52.300
It sort of resembles
an ammonoid.

253
00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:54.540
Cool, huh?

254
00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:09.260
I've got a feeling someone's
been following me for a while.

255
00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:11.100
Nah, couldn't be.

256
00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:28.850
Can't you see I'm busy?!

257
00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:33.120
Collier Coup!

258
00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:43.960
Hm... I don't know
what you're supposed to be,

259
00:16:43.960 --> 00:16:45.960
but I'm guessing you're edible.

260
00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:51.550
Let me see... which one was it?

261
00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:52.650
Maybe...

262
00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.990
Oh, I think I read it recently,
but I don't remember.

263
00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.890
The title's on the
tip of my tongue.

264
00:16:57.890 --> 00:16:59.090
Hm...

265
00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:05.220
Huh. That's weird.

266
00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:07.890
What's a sea king doing on land?

267
00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:13.600
A dinosaur!

268
00:17:13.600 --> 00:17:14.900
Awesome!

269
00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:17.540
No way! This is unreal!

270
00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:18.470
Uh, huh?

271
00:17:18.470 --> 00:17:20.880
Somehow this island
has been frozen in time.

272
00:17:20.880 --> 00:17:23.710
Stuck in the age
of the dinosaurs!

273
00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:24.750
Hm?

274
00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:26.720
Travel in the
Grand Line is so difficult,

275
00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:28.920
so no species ever migrated
between the islands

276
00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:31.820
and their unique ecosystems
were preserved!

277
00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:33.460
Some of these islands
have developed

278
00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:35.620
extremely sophisticated
cultures,

279
00:17:35.620 --> 00:17:38.020
both biological
and sociological.

280
00:17:38.020 --> 00:17:40.820
While others remain in a sort
of evolutionary stagnation,

281
00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:43.210
with little to no progression
for several thousands

282
00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:44.300
or tens of thousands,

283
00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:50.400
or, in this case, it seems,
even millions of years.

284
00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:52.670
I can only assume that
it's the random climates

285
00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:55.140
within the Grand Line
that make this possible.

286
00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:57.740
I mean... What other
explanation is there?

287
00:17:57.740 --> 00:18:00.880
We're standing on the island
that pre-dates mankind.

288
00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:04.430
Luffy!

289
00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:09.690
Are you insane?!

290
00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:12.190
Usopp! Usopp?!

291
00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:15.130
Huh? Nami. What now?

292
00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:17.740
So did you find your book yet?

293
00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:20.400
Uh-huh.

294
00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:31.010
This is bad.

295
00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:32.220
This... island.

296
00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:34.680
What. What's wrong Nami?!

297
00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:57.730
Why do I get the sense
that Nami needs me.

298
00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.540
To those who reside here,

299
00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:05.380
and call this island home,
it must seem as if they've

300
00:19:05.380 --> 00:19:08.380
stumbled upon their
very own private garden.

301
00:19:08.380 --> 00:19:10.380
Thus, I have aptly
named this wondrous,

302
00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:13.620
terrifying place. Little Garden.

303
00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.100
Louis Arnote, Explorer.

304
00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:36.700
<b>Brogy the Giant</b>

305
00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:37.370
Well, what is the answer?

306
00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:39.610
Could you repeat that?
I didn't catch it.

307
00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.540
Please... sir?

308
00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:45.150
I asked if you had any alcohol.

309
00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:47.580
I drank mine.

310
00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:48.920
We have a little.

311
00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:51.340
Oh, you do?! That's perfect!

312
00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:52.620
Um, there's just one thing,

313
00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:53.710
it's not the drinking kind.

314
00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.850
It's for cooking
and disinfecting.

315
00:19:55.850 --> 00:19:57.550
But, if that's acceptable...

316
00:19:57.580 --> 00:19:59.390
...you're... welcome to it all.

317
00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:08.730
A dinosaur!

318
00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.220
I'm Brogy,

319
00:20:25.260 --> 00:20:29.180
the Elbaph's strongest
warrior! Invincible!

320
00:20:34.760 --> 00:20:36.490
Now I have dinner.

321
00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:38.660
And the two of you
are invited as my guests.

322
00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:43.500
Huh?

323
00:20:44.520 --> 00:20:46.460
You okay?

324
00:20:46.460 --> 00:20:48.060
Just
pretend you're dead.

325
00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:50.500
No matter what happens,
don't move a muscle.

326
00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:52.570
But playing
dead only fools bears!

327
00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.540
It won't work!

328
00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:59.010
Huh...

329
00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:06.440
Whoa! What an amazing view!

330
00:21:08.310 --> 00:21:11.710
This is a perfect
spot for our lunch.

331
00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:13.610
We aren't here to
have a picnic, Luffy!

332
00:21:13.610 --> 00:21:15.480
We need to keep moving!

333
00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:17.510
Huh? Oh!

334
00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:19.990
They have active volcanoes here!

335
00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:21.460
Not only that! Look!

336
00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.960
There's a mountain with
huge holes in it!

337
00:21:25.310 --> 00:21:26.390
It's dangerous up there!

338
00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.060
Come down already!

339
00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:39.880
Luffy, no! This is awful!
He's been eaten alive!

340
00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:43.440
Whoa. It got dark.

341
00:21:46.490 --> 00:21:47.850
Cool!

342
00:22:25.370 --> 00:22:31.960
<b>Dorry the Giant</b>

343
00:22:26.790 --> 00:22:28.220
What fun! That was glorious!

344
00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:31.490
Watching the likes of you
grapple with longnecks

345
00:22:31.490 --> 00:22:33.790
is the most entertainment
I've had in quite a while!

346
00:22:33.790 --> 00:22:35.920
You are my first
visitor in a long time.

347
00:22:36.290 --> 00:22:38.880
Wow, you are huge!
Are you human?

348
00:22:42.350 --> 00:22:44.290
Greatest warrior of all Elbaph!

349
00:22:44.290 --> 00:22:45.460
I am Dorry!

350
00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:50.770
It's a... giant!

351
00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:53.570
I've heard that they exist,

352
00:22:53.610 --> 00:22:56.400
but I've never actually
seen one before.

353
00:22:56.400 --> 00:22:57.800
Well, hi! I'm Luffy!

354
00:22:57.800 --> 00:22:58.840
And I'm a pirate!

355
00:23:00.330 --> 00:23:02.930
A pirate?! Well, good
for you, my friend!

356
00:23:04.430 --> 00:23:05.400
Karoo! Wake up!

357
00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:07.900
We have to get out
of here while we can!

358
00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:11.900
By the way, I'd like you to meet
Vivi and Karoo. Say hi to Dorry.

359
00:23:11.900 --> 00:23:15.740
That's great, Luffy!
Just can't shut up!

360
00:23:17.440 --> 00:23:18.410
Tell ya what.

361
00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:21.050
You're all invited to my home!

362
00:23:20.380 --> 00:23:25.510
<b>Home of Brogy the Giant</b>

363
00:23:42.490 --> 00:23:44.530
Go on, eat hearty my friends!

364
00:23:44.530 --> 00:23:46.430
It tastes delicious!

365
00:23:48.700 --> 00:23:51.370
I... I think I've
lost my appetite.

366
00:23:51.370 --> 00:23:53.770
Don't be shy now! Dig in!

367
00:23:55.550 --> 00:23:57.850
– No, I don't wanna eat!
– No, I don't wanna eat!

368
00:23:57.850 --> 00:23:59.350
Huh?

369
00:23:59.350 --> 00:24:00.750
Dinosaur meat is sweet...

370
00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:03.720
I promise you, it's quite tasty.

371
00:24:03.720 --> 00:24:05.670
Well, I guess he's
attempting to fatten us up

372
00:24:05.710 --> 00:24:07.490
before he kills us.

373
00:24:07.490 --> 00:24:08.950
We'll be plump and juicy.

374
00:24:08.950 --> 00:24:10.990
I never thought
it'd end like this.

375
00:24:10.990 --> 00:24:13.500
He's a typical barbaric giant!

376
00:24:13.500 --> 00:24:16.380
We're too young
to die... Too young.

377
00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:18.280
Maybe that's the appeal.

378
00:24:18.280 --> 00:24:20.480
What a waste. It's too bad.

379
00:24:20.480 --> 00:24:24.480
You don't know what a
scrumptious meal you're missing.

380
00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:26.450
We can't eat until
the Log resets...

381
00:24:26.450 --> 00:24:28.590
If we can keep our hunger
and waistlines in check,

382
00:24:28.620 --> 00:24:29.790
we might survive.

383
00:24:29.790 --> 00:24:30.860
Yeah, but...

384
00:24:30.860 --> 00:24:32.900
I don't know how much longer
I can hold out, Nami.

385
00:24:32.900 --> 00:24:34.960
If I don't eat something
pretty soon, I'm not sure

386
00:24:34.960 --> 00:24:37.890
I'll have the strength or
will power to resist his offer.

387
00:24:40.590 --> 00:24:45.360
Brogy, sir? Do you
mind if I ask you a question?

388
00:24:45.360 --> 00:24:47.300
What's on your mind, young lady?

389
00:24:47.300 --> 00:24:49.370
Um, how long will it take

390
00:24:49.410 --> 00:24:51.640
to reset the log on this island?

391
00:24:51.640 --> 00:24:52.510
One full year.

392
00:24:56.180 --> 00:24:59.240
A year... If we waited
that long to eat,

393
00:24:59.270 --> 00:25:01.350
we wouldn't have
stomachs to feed.

394
00:25:01.350 --> 00:25:02.210
It's over.

395
00:25:02.210 --> 00:25:03.880
We have to admit defeat.

396
00:25:03.880 --> 00:25:06.420
Don't tell me you're
gonna fall asleep again!

397
00:25:18.370 --> 00:25:23.330
<b>Home of Dorry the Giant</b>

398
00:25:18.930 --> 00:25:21.630
You sure know
how to cook, giant!

399
00:25:21.630 --> 00:25:23.300
Why, thanks for the compliment.

400
00:25:23.300 --> 00:25:24.670
Your pirate goodies
are excellent, too,

401
00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:25.640
my little friend!

402
00:25:25.640 --> 00:25:27.530
Although the portions
are a little small!

403
00:25:27.530 --> 00:25:29.470
Yeah, I know what ya mean!

404
00:25:30.590 --> 00:25:32.690
But the chef on my ship
made it especially

405
00:25:32.730 --> 00:25:34.760
for this trip, so I'm
glad you liked it.

406
00:25:34.760 --> 00:25:36.530
'Cause otherwise,
I'd have to beat you up!

407
00:25:36.530 --> 00:25:39.500
Was that
a threat... Shorty?

408
00:25:40.970 --> 00:25:43.060
I like you,
little pirate!

409
00:25:43.060 --> 00:25:45.390
You're really funny!

410
00:25:45.390 --> 00:25:47.360
They're becoming fast friends.

411
00:25:47.360 --> 00:25:49.480
Huh. I don't mean to pry,
but why do you choose

412
00:25:49.510 --> 00:25:51.360
to live out here
all by yourself?

413
00:25:51.400 --> 00:25:53.410
Don't you have a
village to call home?

414
00:25:53.800 --> 00:25:55.550
I came from a village...

415
00:25:55.590 --> 00:25:57.670
a place of many
warriors called Elbaph.

416
00:25:57.670 --> 00:26:00.370
It once was home, but I
no longer call it that.

417
00:26:00.370 --> 00:26:01.170
Why?

418
00:26:01.170 --> 00:26:02.480
There are certain
rules in Elbaph,

419
00:26:02.510 --> 00:26:04.050
which must be obeyed.

420
00:26:04.050 --> 00:26:04.950
What kind of rules?

421
00:26:05.590 --> 00:26:07.790
For example,
if a fight breaks out

422
00:26:07.820 --> 00:26:10.560
and neither side yields,
judgment is handed down

423
00:26:10.560 --> 00:26:14.470
by Elbaph's god. Whoever he
deems to be righteous

424
00:26:14.470 --> 00:26:16.790
will be declared the winner
and granted survival

425
00:26:16.820 --> 00:26:18.820
as well as divine protection.

426
00:26:18.820 --> 00:26:21.850
So Elbaph's god decides?
That doesn't seem fair.

427
00:26:21.850 --> 00:26:23.630
Fair or not, all that matters

428
00:26:23.670 --> 00:26:25.790
is this is our battleground.

429
00:26:25.790 --> 00:26:28.490
As on Elbaph, our god will
decide who is righteous

430
00:26:28.490 --> 00:26:31.660
and worthy of winning both
the duel and his life.

431
00:26:32.970 --> 00:26:34.790
We've fought for a century, but,

432
00:26:34.830 --> 00:26:37.100
Elbaph has yet to
choose a champion.

433
00:26:37.950 --> 00:26:40.290
You guys have been fighting
for more than 100 years?!

434
00:26:40.790 --> 00:26:42.700
From a human's point of view,

435
00:26:42.720 --> 00:26:44.160
100 years may seem
like a long time,

436
00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:46.100
but it isn't considering
a giant's average lifespan

437
00:26:46.130 --> 00:26:47.500
is three times yours.

438
00:26:49.170 --> 00:26:50.790
Even with all the
time in the world,

439
00:26:50.810 --> 00:26:51.800
I'd think your desire would wane

440
00:26:51.800 --> 00:26:54.200
after 100 years
of the same battle.

441
00:26:54.200 --> 00:26:56.340
At this point, is there
any real animosity left

442
00:26:56.340 --> 00:26:59.380
between you? Or are you
just fighting to fight?!

443
00:27:06.410 --> 00:27:10.720
Wow, that's
some explosion!

444
00:27:10.720 --> 00:27:13.090
Well then... It's
time to get going.

445
00:27:13.740 --> 00:27:14.280
Huh?

446
00:27:21.660 --> 00:27:22.910
What was that?

447
00:27:22.910 --> 00:27:24.290
An eruption...

448
00:27:27.790 --> 00:27:28.330
Huh?

449
00:27:32.200 --> 00:27:35.520
I don't like that
look. He seems angry.

450
00:27:35.520 --> 00:27:36.990
Please forgive me,

451
00:27:37.020 --> 00:27:39.990
but there is something
I must attend to.

452
00:27:39.990 --> 00:27:42.510
What? You're leaving?

453
00:27:42.510 --> 00:27:43.580
No choice.

454
00:27:43.580 --> 00:27:45.580
That's the signal my
opponent and I use to mark

455
00:27:45.610 --> 00:27:48.010
the beginning of our fight.

456
00:27:48.010 --> 00:27:49.210
A fight?

457
00:27:49.210 --> 00:27:50.710
With whom? Where?

458
00:27:50.710 --> 00:27:52.580
And more importantly, why?

459
00:27:52.580 --> 00:27:53.880
Why?

460
00:27:53.880 --> 00:27:55.280
I don't remember.

461
00:27:59.030 --> 00:28:01.620
And before we realized,
it became our routine.

462
00:28:02.210 --> 00:28:03.910
That volcano is our marker.

463
00:28:03.910 --> 00:28:06.750
Whenever it erupts, we begin.

464
00:28:07.030 --> 00:28:09.170
It's senseless! How
could you have so much

465
00:28:09.170 --> 00:28:12.510
hatred for someone that you'd
fight them for a century?!

466
00:28:12.510 --> 00:28:15.180
What could have happened
to make you this mad?!

467
00:28:15.180 --> 00:28:17.410
Vivi, that's enough!

468
00:28:17.410 --> 00:28:20.010
That's not what
this is about, okay?

469
00:28:26.510 --> 00:28:28.910
You're right.
This is about honor.

470
00:28:37.240 --> 00:28:39.660
I have forgotten...

471
00:28:41.520 --> 00:28:44.100
...the reason for our brawl!

472
00:28:57.690 --> 00:29:01.260
The scope of this planet's so vast and so grand

473
00:29:01.220 --> 00:29:04.610
That if treasure's out there, well where do you start?

474
00:29:04.560 --> 00:29:07.900
Keep your wits about you, don’t leave it to chance

475
00:29:07.920 --> 00:29:12.000
Yeah play it smart but don’t forget
that in the end you’re still rolling the dice

476
00:29:14.040 --> 00:29:15.170
And that's why...

477
00:29:17.910 --> 00:29:21.200
If someone gets in our way, well who cares?

478
00:29:21.250 --> 00:29:24.590
If someone’s running their mouth, well who cares?

479
00:29:24.570 --> 00:29:30.080
Let's sail out, yeah we'll tell all the losers here "bon voyage"

480
00:29:29.840 --> 00:29:31.770
Get lost and stay

481
00:29:31.530 --> 00:29:37.890
Cause even if you think what I'm doing
is dumb, I'm gonna get it done

482
00:29:37.900 --> 00:29:44.470
The more impossible the impressive, reach for the stars

483
00:29:44.580 --> 00:29:51.190
Yeah, even if you think what I'm doing
is dumb, I'm gonna take you on

484
00:29:51.220 --> 00:29:57.860
If we can sail across this vast sea we’ll find a paradise

485
00:29:58.210 --> 00:30:03.570
Go ahead and give it your best,
next time you look out your telescope

486
00:30:03.330 --> 00:30:05.370
You’ll find you’re one step closer
